# Frozen migration baseline seeds: exempt from sqlfluff.
#
# After the per-revision history was collapsed into a single baseline
# per dialect, only these two seed files remain. Each is a verbatim
# copy of the linted schema.sql (see docs/guides/persistence-migrations.md
# "Squash Procedure"), so re-linting it here would be redundant;
# scripts/check_no_edit_migration.sh blocks edits and yoyo's
# content-hash check refuses to re-apply an edited revision, so any
# cosmetic full-ruleset violations could not be remediated anyway.
#
# NEW revisions are deliberately NOT listed: a fresh 14-digit-timestamp
# filename will not match any entry below, so new migrations are held to
# the full ruleset. Add a new revision's path here only if it, too,
# becomes a frozen exception (it should not).
#
# Paths are gitignore-style, relative to this file (repo root). The
# canonical schema.sql files are intentionally absent: they ARE linted.

# SQLite baseline
src/synthorg/persistence/sqlite/revisions/00000000000000_baseline.sql

# Postgres baseline
src/synthorg/persistence/postgres/revisions/00000000000000_baseline.sql
